INT. CHURCH BASEMENT - EVENING

Folding chairs in a circle. A coffee urn. JON (40s) holds a paper cup he has not drunk from. A dozen people. His sponsor, TERRY (60s), sits two seats down.

JON
Ninety-one days. Then one night. So I am back at day four.

Nobody looks away. Terry nods once.

TERRY
Day four is a day. Keep coming back.

EXT. CAR PARK - NIGHT

Jon and Terry lean on Terry's car.

TERRY
What helped last time, before the relapse?

JON
Calling you before, not after. The gym. Telling my sister the truth instead of the version she could handle.

TERRY
Then that is the plan. Recovery is boring on purpose. Call me before.

INT. JON'S SISTER'S HOUSE - DAY

A kitchen full of kids' drawings. Jon's sister PRIYA (30s) is making tea. Jon sits at the table.

JON
I relapsed. Once. I am in the meetings again and Terry knows.

PRIYA
(putting the tea down in front of him)
Thank you for telling me. What do you need from me?

JON
Just this. The tea. Not the speech.

PRIYA
You can have both. But tea first.

INT. CHURCH BASEMENT - EVENING (LATER)

The same circle. Jon's cup is empty this time.

JON
Day thirty. Again. It counts.

TERRY
It counts.

END CARD: Support for addiction and recovery is available. In the U.S., call or text 988 or contact SAMHSA's National Helpline. Help is available.
